cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ContextSafe, please cite it as below."
title: "ContextSafe — offline synthetic fixture validator and deterministic evaluator for transgender and nonbinary patient-safety release gating"
abstract: >-
  A clinically and community-governed release-gate plan, with a bounded offline
  implementation slice: strict versioned schemas for synthetic patient cases and
  observations, a fail-closed deterministic evaluator where missing or ambiguous
  evidence is indeterminate, unsigned governance-contract compilation, and a
  recoverable synthetic-evidence store producing hash-covered JSON receipts.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Chelsea
    family-names: Kelly-Reif
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ChelseaKR/contextsafe"
keywords:
  - patient-safety
  - transgender-health
  - health-informatics
  - hl7-fhir
  - synthetic-data
  - release-gating
  - deterministic-evaluation
